# Third-party / licensed tools. KEEP LOCAL — never committed.
#
# FoldX ships under the CRG Academic License: free for academic use, but the grant is
# non-transferable and scoped to "computers and/or servers at their research site" for research
# purposes. Committing tools/foldx_linux/foldx_20261231 redistributes an 82.7 MB licensed binary,
# and rotabase.txt and molecules/*.json are part of the same licensed distribution. README.md
# already tells users to register at foldxsuite.crg.eu and install FoldX themselves, which is the
# correct distribution path, so tracking any of it contradicts the README.
#
# The `!` negations that used to re-include these files are what made the previous comment ("do not
# commit binaries or downloads") untrue. They were deliberately removed: the folder patterns below
# now cover everything with no exceptions.
tools/foldx/
tools/foldx_linux/
tools/p2rank/

# Dev scratch scripts
scratch/

# Recovered session transcripts and the decoder that produced them: evidence, not
# source. ~45 MB of decoded .jsonl — kept on disk deliberately, never committed.
.session-recovery/

# OS / editor cruft
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Build artifacts (root-level esbuild output removed by `npm run clean`, Vite cache)
/server.js
.vite/

# Python bytecode. Checkpoints and model weights are third-party artefacts carrying their own
# terms, so they are kept local on the same reasoning as the licensed tools above: a fresh clone
# and a fresh VM fetch them rather than inherit them from git. The `!` negations that used to
# re-include the ThermoMPNN and ESM weights are deliberately gone.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pth
*.pt
.venv/
tools/.venv/
tools/vesm/
tools/thermompnn/__pycache__/
tools/thermompnn/.idea/
tools/thermompnn/data_all/
tools/thermompnn/dataset_splits/


data/*.csv
data/*.sqlite*
data/*.json
data/dgtex-v1-input/

# Repowise cache and databases
.repowise/

# Graphify knowledge graph outputs & caches
graphify-out/
.graphify/

# Graft context graph cache
/graft/
.ignore

# zvec-grep index and local embedding models
.zvec-grep/

# Local secrets
.sidecar_secret

# Deployment runbook, kept local. It documents the OCI host, the deployment topology, and the shape
# of the production secrets. Every credential in it is a placeholder (<YOUR_CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN>,
# <32_byte_hex_token>), but the host is real -- it appears as OCI_SSH_HOST's example, 92.5.173.166 --
# so it does not belong in a repository that is public.
#
# UNTRACKING THIS DOES NOT HIDE IT. As of 2026-09-29 the file is still present in history on main and
# on all four claude/* branches, so publishing the repo would still expose the host. Removing it for
# real needs git-filter-repo, and on this repository that means a rewrite plus a fresh repository,
# because GitHub's refs/pull/* are read-only and keep pointing at the old commits.
doc/DEPLOYMENT_OCI.md

# Local editor and workspace caches
.commandcode/
.freebuff/
.zcode/
/rotabase.txt
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
impeccable-detect.*

tools/graft/

.empryo

# brand-mark rasteriser profile
tools/brand-mark/.browser-profile/

# Container-local worker role and host-local deployment journal
.deployment-role*
/deploy/runtime/

# Machine-local agent/tooling config (paths are absolute to one checkout)
/.codex/config.toml
/.dsh-validate-yaml.cjs

# compute:benchmark structure cache (AlphaFold models, re-downloaded on demand)
data/benchmark-structures/

